# Emperor of Bones: the creature card it returns is put onto the battlefield without being cast, so Bot2's Containment
# Priest ("if a nontoken creature would enter and it wasn't cast, exile it instead") exiles it. At turn 3's combat the
# Emperor exiles the Llanowar Elves; Adapt 2 puts counters on it, the trigger tries to return the Elves, and they are
# exiled again (a new object): nothing new is on the battlefield, so there is no finality counter and nothing to sacrifice.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Emperor of Bones
Llanowar Elves
Lightning Bolt
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Containment Priest
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Emperor of Bones.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Containment Priest.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Graveyard.Llanowar Elves)
[T3 Bot1.BeginCombat]
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Emperor of Bones.Activate(Ability: Adapt)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile = Llanowar Elves
Bot1.Battlefield.Emperor of Bones.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
Stack.Count = 0
